  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\omega(\\neq 1)$ be a cubic root of unity. Then the minimum value of the set $\\left\\{\\left|a+b \\omega+c \\omega^2\\right|^2 ; a, b, c\\right.$ are distinct non-zero integers} equals"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$15$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$5$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$3$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$4$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\left|a+b \\omega+c \\omega^2\\right|^2=a^2+b^2+c^2-a b-b c-c a$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& =\\frac{1}{2}\\left[(a-b)^2+(b-c)^2+(c-a)^2\\right] \\\\\n& \\therefore \\operatorname{Min}=\\frac{1+1+4}{2}=3 \\quad(a, b, c \\in\\{1,2,3\\})\n\\end{aligned}$"
  }
